<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">All-India Muslim League</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1906</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Muslim League</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The All-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Muslim League was a political party founded at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dhaka">Dhaka</a> in 1906 to represent the interests of Muslims in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a>. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-jinnah">Muhammad Ali Jinnah</a> it adopted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lahore-resolution">Lahore Resolution</a> of 1940 calling for separate Muslim states, and its success in the 1946 elections led to the creation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1947, after which it became the ruling party there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/all-india-muslim-league.jpg" alt="All-India Muslim League" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash wki · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pakistan_Star%26Crescent.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
